  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The political landscape in Indonesia is currently focused on the identification of a successor for the vice presidential role following the departure of Gibran Rakabuming Raka. Recent reports indicate that President Prabowo Subianto intends to finalize and submit a list of at least two potential nominees to the relevant authorities no later than November 25. While internal figures from the Gerindra party remain at the forefront of media speculation, other high-profile individuals and regional leaders have also been mentioned as candidates. Spokespersons for the administration have emphasized that the final decision rests with the President, who is expected to conduct thorough discussions with members of the coalition parties. Key criteria for the position include strong political experience and unwavering dedication to the administration's policy direction, as the selection process continues to generate significant discourse among political observers and coalition partners.",
